{
  "slug": "enhance",
  "name": "Enhance",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Master enhancement orchestrator: 7 specialized analyzers run in parallel and produce a unified report with certainty-graded findings. `/enhance:agent` analyzes agent frontmatter and tool restrictions; `/enhance:prompt` general prompt patterns; `/enhance:docs` RAG-readiness; `/enhance:plugin` MCP/security patterns; `/enhance:claudemd` project-memory files; `/enhance:hooks` hook safety; `/enhance:skills` SKILL.md trigger quality. HIGH-certainty issues are auto-fixable with `--fix`. Per-analyzer model selection (Opus for quality-critical analysis, Sonnet for pattern-matching) keeps token costs predictable. Designed to plug into /next-task and /prepare-delivery as a pre-ship gate.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **9 skills**, **8 agents** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (9): `enhance-agent-prompts` (Use when improving agent prompts, frontmatter, and tool restrictions), `enhance-claude-memory` (Use when improving CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md project memory files), `enhance-cross-file` (Use when checking cross-file consistency: tools vs frontmatter, agent references, duplicate rules, contradictions), `enhance-docs` (Use when improving documentation structure, accuracy, and RAG readiness), `enhance-hooks` (Use when reviewing hooks for safety, timeouts, and correct frontmatter), `enhance-orchestrator` (Use when coordinating multiple enhancers for /enhance command), `enhance-plugins` (Use when analyzing plugin structures, MCP tools, and plugin security patterns), `enhance-prompts` (Use when improving general prompts for structure, examples, and constraints), and 1 more\n- **Agents** (8): `agent-enhancer` (Analyze agent prompts for optimization opportunities), `claudemd-enhancer` (Analyzes and optimizes CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md project memory files for better AI understanding), `cross-file-enhancer` (Analyze cross-file semantic consistency (tools, agents, rules)), `docs-enhancer` (Analyze documentation for readability and RAG optimization), `hooks-enhancer` (Analyze hook definitions for safety and best practices), `plugin-enhancer` (Analyze plugin structures and MCP tool definitions), `prompt-enhancer` (Analyze prompts for prompt engineering best practices), `skills-enhancer` (Analyze SKILL.md files for trigger and structure quality)\n- **Commands** (1): `enhance` (Analyze plugins, agents, prompts, docs, hooks, and skills for best-practice gaps)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install enhance@claude-community` from `agent-sh/enhance`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 9,
    "agent": 8,
    "command": 1
  },
